{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790361405,"nonce":"eCHUjEHY09sr0jEwG2WfdTzQIQo=","title":"Interpreter saves a float into an async slot by value and loads it back by bits","message":"In the bytecode interpreter (crates/compiler/src/hir_interp.rs, `run_frame`), `Op::AsyncSaveSlot` converts the value with `value_to_i64`, which turns `Float` and `F32` into integers with `as i64`. `Op::AsyncLoadSlot` reads the slot back with `read_typed`, which reinterprets the stored bits as f64 or f32. Cranelift and the wasm backend store the bit pattern. A float live across an await in a poll function the interpreter runs reloads as an unrelated value; on wasm every poll function stays in the interpreter, since the wasm JIT hook in crates/zyntax_wasm/src/lib.rs only takes parameterless functions. Found by reading; not reproduced.\n\nDone: the interpreter stores float slots as their bits, matching the compiled tiers, and an async test keeps an f64 live across an await under the interpreter.","files":null}]}